    {
      "id": "17876",
      "key": "SFCC-40",
      "summary": "Coupon Code Management",
      "description": "As a\n Site Merchandiser or Client Services team member, \n\n\nI want \nto create and manage coupon codes in SFCC Business Manager, \n\n\nso that\n promotional codes can be issued for campaigns and one-off customer situations without requiring a code deployment.\nCampaign coupon codes (Site Merchandiser): \nMerchandisers create coupon codes as part of a promotion campaign in BM. Three code types are supported:\nSingle-use unique codes — each code can only be redeemed once, by one customer\nGeneric multi-use codes — one code redeemable by multiple customers (e.g. a seasonal campaign code)\nBulk unique codes — a batch of single-use codes imported via CSV, used for large-scale campaigns or direct mail\nOne-off customer service codes (Client Services): \nCS team members create individual promotion codes in BM to resolve specific customer situations — for example a goodwill gesture, a shipping correction, or a complaint resolution. These codes must be auditable so that CS management can track what codes were issued, by whom, and against which customer interaction. Confirmed with Cayley (CS team).\n\n\nCS team members require a configured BM role with sufficient permissions to create promotion codes without access to broader merchandising functions. Role configuration is covered in the User Management & Reporting epic.",
