    {
      "id": "17847",
      "key": "SFCC-21",
      "summary": "NFRs & Observability",
      "description": "Epic Summary\n\n\nThis epic defines and implements the platform-wide non-functional requirements for the Zimmermann SFCC implementation, and establishes the observability, monitoring, and alerting capabilities required to operate the platform in production across all 8 regional storefronts. NFR standards will be agreed with Zimmermann prior to implementation and will cover areas including performance, availability, security, and accessibility.\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\n\nZimmermann's current Magento platform has known performance constraints including site speed issues, Core Web Vitals failures, and unstable caching and indexing. Defining and validating NFRs on the new SFCC platform ensures it meets Zimmermann's brand and client experience standards at global scale, and that the team has the visibility needed to detect and respond to issues in production from day one.\nScope\nIn Scope\nDefinition and sign-off of platform-wide NFR standards in collaboration with Zimmermann, covering areas including performance, scalability, availability, security, and accessibility\nValidation of the platform against agreed NFR targets prior to go-live across all 8 regional storefronts\nObservability tooling setup: error monitoring, performance monitoring, and alerting for the production SFCC and PWA Kit environments\nIncident response thresholds and alerting runbooks agreed with Zimmermann for post-launch operations\nOut of Scope\nUAT, penetration testing, and formal performance testing execution — Zimmermann responsibility\nGTM/analytics tagging and data layer instrumentation — covered in SFCC-22 SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing\nCI/CD pipeline setup and environment provisioning — covered in SFCC-1 Platform Setup & Environments\nPost-launch performance optimisation and ongoing monitoring operations — Zimmermann/hypercare responsibility\nDependencies\nSFCC-1 Platform Setup & Environments — environment infrastructure must be in place before performance baselines can be established\nSFCC-2 PWA Kit Components — NFR validation is a cross-cutting concern; component and feature builds across other epics must be sufficiently complete before end-to-end validation can run\nZimmermann — NFR targets must be agreed and signed off before implementation and validation work begins\nAssumptions & Constraints\nNFR targets have not yet been formally defined or signed off; this epic cannot be fully scoped until Zimmermann confirms acceptance criteria\nThird-party widget compliance (e.g. Didomi banner, Global-e checkout iframe) is the responsibility of the respective vendors\nThe NFR deliverable from the discovery phase has not yet been published; this epic will be updated once that document is available\nPriority:\n Medium\nTarget Release / Sprint:\n Sprint 7",
