      "id": "17846",
      "key": "SFCC-20",
      "summary": "Data Migration",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Data Migration\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the migration of product data from AP21 and enriched product data from Magento into SFCC, customer email and Omneo ID migration, URL strategy and 301 redirects, technical SEO implementation, and the foundations for GEO enablement. All other customer data is sourced live from Omneo at login — not migrated.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nA clean migration, preserved URL structure, and correctly implemented SEO technical foundations are essential to protect Zimmermann's organic search ranking and ensure continuity of customer data at go-live.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nProduct data migration from AP21 via MuleSoft, with enriched product data sourced from Magento for initial load\nCustomer email and Omneo ID migration only; passwords and saved cards are not migrated\nContentful API reconfiguration to point to the new SFCC platform\nURL strategy — preservation of existing locale prefixes and product URL format (.html suffix)\n301 redirect implementation for all changed URLs, managed at CDN/edge level\nTechnical SEO — canonical tags, hreflang, XML sitemaps, robots.txt, SSR, title tags, meta descriptions, H1 hierarchy, structured data (Product, CollectionPage, LocalBusiness, Organisation schemas)\nGEO technical foundations (SSR, structured data, canonical URLs, sitemaps)\nOut of Scope:\nProduct image/asset migration to CDN — out of scope\nHistorical order migration — order history sourced live from NewStore/Omneo via MuleSoft\nSEO strategy and content optimisation — Zimmermann/Sparro scope\nCDN redirect rule management post-launch — Zimmermann scope\nDependencies\nMuleSoft/AP21 — product data feed for migration\nMagento — enriched product data source for initial load\nOmneo — customer identity source; email and Omneo ID migrated, all other data sourced live at login\nContentful — CMS connection reconfiguration\nCloudflare/CDN — redirect rule carry-forward from existing setup\nAssumptions & Constraints\nCustomer passwords cannot be migrated; customers must reset on first login\nSaved payment cards cannot be migrated; customers re-enter at next purchase\nProduct image URLs are preserved from existing CDN; no asset re-migration required\nUp to 3 mock migration cycles in non-production environments are in scope per the SOW, ahead of production cutover",
