|\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SFCC BM | UAT org | Merch sign-off, production-mirrored config |\n| MRT / PWA | MRT UAT | Business acceptance testing, all 6 regions |\n| 3P systems | All systems real | Same as STAGE |\n| OMS SIT | Feeds UAT | No further OMS SIT required after STAGE |\n\n* Deploys from: manual trigger — requires business stakeholder sign-off per region.\n\nTier 6 — PRODUCTION\n-------------------\n\n| Layer | Environment | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SFCC BM | PROD org | Live BM config — AU first, then wave rollout |\n| MRT / PWA | MRT Production | AU canary → all regions via `mrt:activate` |\n| 3P systems | All PROD systems | Live credentials, live data |\n| OMS SIT | Feeds PROD | NewStore PROD activated with Digital wave rollout |\n\n* Deploys from: release manager only — manual approval gate in GitHub Environments.\n* Canary: AU goes first; remaining regions open only after error rate < 0.5% over 2h on AU.\n* Rollback: `mrt:activate --target production --bundle-id <PREVIOUS_ID>`. 50-bundle retention (~30-day window).\n\nBranch → Environment → Trigger matrix\n-------------------------------------\n\n| Branch | Tier | Trigger | Gate |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `feature/*` | LOCAL (developer machine — no MRT deployment) | `npm start` | None — fast iteration |\n| `develop` | DEV (MRT staging) | Merge to `develop` | Vitest + Storybook interaction tests + Playwright P0 + bundle size + MuleSoft contract tests + Lighthouse CI + LHCI trend gate |\n| `develop` | SIT (MRT sit) | After `sit-gate` passes on `develop` | Digital SIT Gate green |\n| `release/v*.*.*` | STAGE (MRT pre-prod) | Manual | Jira booking confirmed, Digital SIT green, OMS SIT complete |\n| `release/v*.*.*` | UAT (MRT UAT) | Manual | Business stakeholder sign-off |\n| `main` | PROD (MRT Production) | Manual | Release manager approval, post-canary smoke |\n| `hotfix/*` | PROD (expedited) | Merge to `main` | Abbreviated pipeline, approval gate retained |\n\nGitHub Environment secret scope\n-------------------------------\n\n| GitHub Environment | Secrets scoped | Requires reviewer |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `staging` | Dev credentials | No |\n| `sit` | SIT credentials | Yes — Zimmermann environment owner |\n| `pre-prod` | Pre-prod credentials | Yes — Zimmermann environment owner |\n| `uat` | UAT credentials | Yes — Zimmermann stakeholder |\n| `production` | PROD credentials | Yes — Release manager |\n\nSIT secrets must be scoped to the `sit` GitHub Environment only — they must not be accessible to the `production` environment workflow.\n\nOpen dependencies\n-----------------\n\n1. **NewStore notification channel** — the deploy-SIT path currently only echoes to the Actions log on success. Wire to Slack webhook, email, or Jira comment once NewStore confirms their preferred channel.\n2. **MuleSoft contract test spec source** — `test:contracts` is a placeholder. MuleSoft must publish OpenAPI specs (or expose a contract endpoint in SIT) before the contract gate is active. This is the same dependency tracked on the MuleSoft row of [7.1b Third Party Credentials](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/268337165) — update status there, not as a separate Jira item.\n3. **OMS SIT sign-off mechanism** — STAGE entry criteria requires NewStore to formally sign off OMS SIT completion on a Jira ticket. The sign-off field on that ticket type needs to be configured by the Zimmermann Jira admin.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

